{
  "$comment": "One corpus, two languages, for the URLs a `sealed` WebhookEndpoint may hold. `pattern` is whether sms_webhook::SEALABLE_URL_PATTERN accepts the text as typed (the database's CHECK is that pattern, and the console's early check is its TypeScript twin, frontends/packages/gateway/src/webhook-rules.ts); `sealable` is whether the worker can also seal for it, that is the pattern AND delivery_route (URL parsing) agreeing. Rows with pattern true and sealable false are the ones the pattern alone lets through, which `@uri` and the worker's delivery_route refuse. sms-webhook's tests/sealable_url_cases.rs and the gateway package's webhook-rules.test.ts both read this file. Add a row when a URL surprises either side.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.vaam.store/webhooks/vsms",
      "pattern": true,
      "sealable": true,
      "why": "the usual receiver"
    },
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:9000/webhooks",
      "pattern": true,
      "sealable": true,
      "why": "plain http with a port"
    },
    {
      "url": "HTTPS://Example.COM/Hook",
      "pattern": true,
      "sealable": true,
      "why": "the scheme and host are case-insensitive, the path is not folded"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://example.com",
      "pattern": true,
      "sealable": true,
      "why": "no path is the root route"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://example.com/",
      "pattern": true,
      "sealable": true,
      "why": "the root route"
    },
    {
